---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "3D Printing Materials"
description: "Explore our FDM and resin materials — PLA, PETG, ABS/ASA, Nylon, TPU, carbon-filled filaments and high-detail resins. UK-based printing with material guidance."
---

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Bondar Labs · Materials</p>
    <h1>3D printing materials</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Choosing the right material matters as much as the model. We’ll recommend the best option based on strength, heat exposure,
      flexibility, surface finish and how the part will be used.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ '/quote/' | url }}">Get a Quote</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="{{ '/services/' | url }}">Explore Services</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="grid grid-2">

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-body prose">
          <h2>Quick material picker</h2>
          <p class="muted">
            Not sure where to start? This is a practical guide. If your use case is unusual, send the brief and we’ll recommend the best match.
          </p>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Use case</th>
                <th>Typical choice</th>
                <th>Why</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Fast prototypes / visual parts</td>
                <td>PLA</td>
                <td>Clean print quality, great detail, wide colour choice</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Everyday functional parts</td>
                <td>PETG</td>
                <td>Tougher feel than PLA, good all-round performance</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Outdoor / UV exposure</td>
                <td>ASA</td>
                <td>Better weather and UV resistance for outdoor components</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Wear / fatigue / mechanical use</td>
                <td>Nylon</td>
                <td>Engineering material for demanding functional parts (geometry dependent)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Flexible parts</td>
                <td>TPU</td>
                <td>Rubber-like flexibility for grips, bumpers and seals</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>High detail & smooth surfaces</td>
                <td>Resin (MSLA)</td>
                <td>Excellent detail for miniatures, stamps, masters and small precision parts</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <p class="muted">
            Looking for the lowest-cost option where suitable? PLA (FDM) and grey water-washable resin (MSLA) are often great starting points.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-body prose">
          <h2>Colours and sourcing</h2>
          <p>
            We keep a wide stock of popular colours and can source specific materials on request.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>PLA:</strong> large in-stock colour range (around 50 shades).</li>
            <li><strong>PETG:</strong> a core range of common colours (around 10).</li>
            <li><strong>Engineering filaments (ABS/ASA/Nylon/TPU):</strong> typically stocked in black/white/natural; other options can be sourced.</li>
            <li><strong>Resin:</strong> water-washable grey by default (also black/white/clear stocked); other colours on request.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="muted">
            If colour or brand matters, mention it in your quote request — we’ll confirm availability and lead time before printing.
          </p>

          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ '/quote/' | url }}">Get a Quote</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="{{ '/services/fdm/' | url }}">FDM Printing</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="card mt-16">
      <div class="card-body prose">
        <h2>Materials we offer</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          These pages keep things practical: when to choose a material, what to expect, and common trade-offs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top:16px">
      {% for m in collections.materials %}
        <a class="card card-link" href="{{ m.url | url }}">
          <div class="card-body">
            <div class="kicker">{{ m.data.category }}</div>
            <h2 class="h3">{{ m.data.title }}</h2>
            <p class="muted">{{ m.data.summary }}</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    {% include "partials/cta-wide.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>